I have everything from the specs. One thing to nail down first: a scenario where a pipe is passed with `|vy| > GLIDE_VY` (bonus NOT awarded), so that test pins both branches of the bonus rule. Searching for one:
Good candidates. Verifying the chosen scenario (seed=1, flaps=`0000101`) tick-by-tick before pinning it in a test:
The scenario has been verified against my manual simulation (at t=45, y=794, vy=+45 → only +1 point; the other three paths are +2 each → 7 points). Now I'll create the test suite:
All 19 pass. Quick negative control — mutating the tick order in a copy to prove the suite catches regressions:
That swap was unobservable (physics and scroll touch disjoint state) — a weak mutation. Testing the real spec violations: collision-before-scroll, and position-only scoring:
Mutation 1 didn't trigger — suspicious. Verifying the mutation was actually applied:
The mutation is applied yet behavior is unchanged — need to see what's actually happening:
Still 41 — my mental model of the mutation's effect is wrong somewhere. Instrumenting:
At tick 40 pre-scroll x=400 can't hit — yet it dies there. Tracing `alive` per step:
Found it — my mutation was malformed: the `replace` left the original post-scroll collision block in place, so the engine still collided after scroll. Redoing it properly:
The mutation is caught now — but the restored run also failed. Investigating:
`engine.py` matches the backup, yet behavior says collision-before-scroll — inspecting what the backup actually contains:
Found it — a classic CPython pitfall: my "mutation" was the same size as the original (just line moves), and everything happened within the same wall-clock second, so `int(mtime)` matched and Python kept using the **stale mutated `.pyc`** from `__pycache__`. The source is correct; the cache is lying. Clearing it:
Suite is green on the true original. Re-running both negative controls with clean caches to confirm they're valid:
Both mutations are now properly detected. Final end-to-end sanity (demo diff + selfcheck), since engine.py was touched during mutation testing:
DONE

`test_flapsim.py` — 19 stdlib `unittest` tests, all passing:

- **Physics clamps (5)**: flap sets vy (not adds), plain gravity tick, `VY_MAX` clamp, soft ceiling zeroing vy, fatal floor clamping y without zeroing vy
- **LCG/world (5)**: exact LCG values incl. wraparound, spawn advances the LCG exactly once with the spec gap formula, spawn only on `t % SPAWN_EVERY == 0`, scroll, cull boundary (`x + PIPE_W <= 0`)
- **AABB edges (3)**: half-open touching edges both orientations, bird bottom exactly at `gap_top + GAP_H` survives / one centi-unit below dies, horizontal no-overlap at both pipe edges
- **Clean-glide bonus (2)**: both branches — seed 7/`0010` first pass at t=45 with vy=+27 scores 2; seed 1/`0000101` first pass at t=45 with vy=+45 scores only 1 (verified against an independent hand simulation), final score 7 = 1+2+2+2
- **Per-tick order (4)**: ceiling-pinned bird dies exactly on the tick a pipe scrolls into it (pins spawn-at-t=0 + scroll-before-collision), fatal tick counted in `ticks_run` and run halts, pipe scored exactly once (position-only scoring would give 56, not 8), zero-tick initial state

Mutation-tested the suite: collision-before-scroll and position-only-scoring variants each fail the right tests; restored engine re-passes all 19. Demo output remains byte-identical to spec/09 and `--selfcheck` is all OK. (One detour worth noting: an intermediate "mutation not caught" turned out to be a stale same-size `.pyc` from second-granularity mtime caching — cleared `__pycache__` and re-verified.)

